\nDownload file PDFRead file\n\n## Abstract\n\nIn 2018 Coll, Mayers, and Mayers conjectured that the q-series $( q, -q^3; q^4 )_\\infty^{-1}$ is the generating function for a certain parity statistic related to the index of seaweed algebras. We prove this conjecture. Thanks to earlier work by Seo and Yee, the conjecture would follow from the non-negativity of the coefficients of this infinite product. Using a variant of the circle method along with Euler-Maclaurin summation, we establish this non-negativity, thereby confirming the Coll-Mayers-Mayers Conjecture.\n\nPublic Full-text 1\n\nContent uploaded by William Craig\n\nAuthor content\n\nAll content in this area was uploaded by William Craig on May 07, 2023\n\nContent may be subject to copyright.\n\narXiv:2112.09269v5 [math.CO] 23 Aug 2022\n\nSEAWEED ALGEBRAS AND THE INDEX STATISTIC FOR PARTITIONS\n\nWILLIAM CRAIG\n\nAbstract. In 2018 Coll, Mayers, and Mayers conjectured that the q-series q, −q 3;q 4−1\n\n∞is the gener-\n\nating function for a certain parity statistic related to the index of seaweed algebras. We prove this con-\n\njecture. Thanks to earlier work by Seo and Yee, the conjecture would follow from the non-negativity of\n\nthe coeﬃcients of this inﬁnite product. Using a variant of the circle method along with Euler–Maclaurin\n\nsummation, we establish this non-negativity, thereby conﬁrming the Coll–Mayers–Mayers Conjecture.\n\n1. Introduction and Statement of Results\n\nRecall that a partition λ of the non-negative integer n is a non-increasing sequence of positive\n\nintegers λ= (λ 1≥λ 2≥ ·· · ≥ λ k) which sum to n. We adopt the usual convention that the empty set\n\nis the only partition of zero. Deﬁne the q-series G(q) by\n\nG(q) := X\n\nn≥0\n\na(n)q n:= 1\n\n(q, −q 3;q 4)∞\n\n,\n\nwhere (a;q)∞:= Q∞\n\nn=0 (1 −aq n) and (a, b;q)∞:= (a;q)∞(b;q)∞. into odd parts whose index is even, and likewise o n as the number of partitions of n into odd parts\n\nwhose index is odd. With this notation, the conjecture of Coll, Mayers, and Mayers may be stated as\n\nfollows.\n\nColl–Mayers–Mayers Conjecture. The following are true:\n\n(1) All the coeﬃcients of G(q)are non-negative.\n\n(2) We have G(q) = P\n\nn≥0|e n−o n|q n.\n\n2020 Mathematics Subject Classiﬁcation. 05A15, 11P82.\n\nKey words and phrases. Index of partitions, non-negative coeﬃcients, seaweed algebras, circle method.\n\n1\n\n2 WILLIAM CRAIG\n\nIn recent years, several papers have made progress towards proving this conjecture. Seo and Yee\n\n[10] proved that (1) implies the full Coll–Mayers–Mayers Conjecture 1. After this work, Chern [3]\n\ndemonstrated using the circle method that a(n)≥0 for all n > 2.4×10 14 and veriﬁed the non-\n\nnegativity by computer for 0 ≤n≤10000. In this paper, we use a modiﬁed approach, involving a\n\ndiﬀerent version of the circle method and Euler-Maclaurin summation, which reduces the last possible\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nNavid Tafaghodi Khajavi (https://www.catalyzex.com/author/Navid%20Tafaghodi%20Khajavi)\nciteturn0search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 5 months ago; Authors:Navid Tafaghodi Khajavi, Anthony Kuh ... The Cholesky decomposition enables us to achieve a tree structure factor graph at each cascade stage of the algorithm which facilitates the use of the message passing algorithm since the approximated graph has less loops compared to the original graph. ... Here, we present theoretical result that guarantees the convergence of the proposed model approximation using the cascade of tree decompositions.\n\n# Navid Tafaghodi Khajavi\n\n## Model Approximation Using Cascade of Tree Decompositions\n\nRequest Code\n\nImage: Bookmark button\n\nImage: Alert button\n\nAug 10, 2018\n\nAuthors:Navid Tafaghodi Khajavi, Anthony Kuh\n\nFigures and Tables:\n\nImage: Figure 1 for Model Approximation Using Cascade of Tree Decompositions\n\nImage: Figure 2 for Model Approximation Using Cascade of Tree Decompositions\n\nImage: Figure 3 